<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>The Honduran-Cuban War - March 12, 1968</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;This scenario is set in an alternate history timeline.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;The Point of Divergence is in 1955&amp;nbsp;when&amp;nbsp;large quantities of iridium are discovered in Honduras.&amp;nbsp; Iridium is very useful for a variety of industrial applications.&amp;nbsp; It is also rare and extremely valuable.&amp;nbsp; Honduras, which suddenly found itself in possession of most of the world's accessible supply of iridium, quickly took advantage of its new wealth to become a regional power, purchasing military aircraft, a flotilla of small warships, and even a submarine from the United States.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;Honduras has an uneasy relationship with some of the other nations in the region.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Its closest allies are Costa Rica and the newly independent nation of Jamaica.&amp;nbsp; Relations with Mexico are generally friendly, but are strained at times because of economic reasons.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;Relations with Cuba have deteriorated since the Communist Revolution in that country.&amp;nbsp; Since 1965, there have been a number of&amp;nbsp;incidents in the Caribbean and in the Yucatán Channel.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;By&amp;nbsp;1968, tensions with Cuba have reached a breaking point.&amp;nbsp; When a Cuban patrol boat fired on a Honduran fishing boat that had strayed too close to (but, according to Honduras, not within) Cuban waters, a Honduran destroyer first requested it break off its attack.&amp;nbsp; When it was clear the&amp;nbsp;Cubans had no intention of ceasing their attack and that&amp;nbsp;civilian lives were in peril, the Hondruans&amp;nbsp;sank the Cuban warship.&amp;nbsp; Cuba has declared this &lt;EM&gt;casus belli &lt;/EM&gt;and that it is preparing for war.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt"&gt;-------------------------------------------------------&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = "o" ns = "urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt"&gt;A delta template .ini file has been included in the .zip file to assist in updating the scenario to any future versions of the database.&amp;nbsp; &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt"&gt;Scenario Author: Mark Gellis&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt"&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
